Given series: 4, 25, 121, ?, 529, 961

The pattern followed here is:

The series given above is squares of the alternate prime numbers.

Prime numbers: **2**, 3, **5**, 7, **11**, 13, __**17**__, 19, **23**, 29,** 31**

2² = 4;

5² = 25;

11² = 121;

**17² = 289**;

23² = 529;

31² = 961

Hence, ‘289’ is the correct answer.

questions.question:
A + B means ‘A is the sister of B’;

A - B means ‘A is the father of B’;

A × B means ‘A is the son of B’;

A ÷ B means ‘A is the Wife of B’

If, E ÷ F - H + J ÷ G × D, then how is E related to G?

questions.solution:
The pattern followed here is:

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/2e1a2f0dc142ecfb544963c2209981c3e759d0cf81e91577dd86d50c0a2dc835.png] 

W - 6 → Q;

Q - 5 → **L**;

L - 4 → H;

H - 3 → E;

E - 2 → C

Hence, ‘L’ is the correct answer.
